From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: hidapi: let libusb reach Xbox 360 / Xbox One pads

The libusb whitelist (on whenever hidraw is available) only lets the
GameCube adapter through, so SDL's Xbox 360 and Xbox One drivers never see
wired pads on Linux: those interfaces are vendor class (0xff), have no
hidraw node, and libusb is the only way to them. Pads such as the 8BitDo
Ultimate 2C wait for the player-LED command these drivers send, and stay
silent on a kernel whose xpad has no LED support. HID-class devices keep
going through hidraw as before.

--- a/src/hidapi/SDL_hidapi.c
+++ b/src/hidapi/SDL_hidapi.c
@@ -1274,7 +1274,10 @@
 #endif
         for (usb_dev = usb_devs; usb_dev; usb_dev = usb_dev->next) {
             if (use_libusb_whitelist) {
-                if (!IsInWhitelist(usb_dev->vendor_id, usb_dev->product_id)) {
+                /* Xbox 360 and Xbox One interfaces (vendor class) have no
+                   hidraw node, so libusb is the only way SDL reaches them. */
+                if (!IsInWhitelist(usb_dev->vendor_id, usb_dev->product_id) &&
+                    usb_dev->interface_class != 0xff) {
 #ifdef DEBUG_HIDAPI
                     SDL_Log("Device was not in libusb whitelist: %ls %ls 0x%.4hx 0x%.4hx",
                             usb_dev->manufacturer_string, usb_dev->product_string,
